= Reward =

<ul>
<li>{{:Jeweled Skull}}</li>
</ul>

= Summary =
{{CheckboxList}}
* Find [[Yiz Pon]] in the northeast corner of [[Western Karana]].
* Say 'What beasts?' to [[Yiz Pon]] to receive [[Torn Parchment (Letter to Hyrill Pon)]] and spawn [[a Splitpaw assassin]].
* Kill [[a Splitpaw assassin]] and loot a [[Hollow Skull (Skull of Wun Toque)]] (container with two slots).
* ''(Optional)'' Give [[Torn Parchment]] to [[Hyrill Pon]] in [[Freeport|West Freeport]].
* Kill [[Lynuga]] in [[Innothule Swamp]] and loot a [[Large Ruby]].
* Kill [[Kurrpok Splitpaw]] in [[Splitpaw Lair]] or [[Southern Karana]] and loot a [[Ruby Pendant]].
* Combine the [[Large Ruby]] and [[Ruby Pendant]] in the [[Hollow Skull (Skull of Wun Toque)]] to create the [[Jeweled Skull]].
{{End}}

= Walkthrough =
[[Yiz Pon]] spawns in the far northeast corner of [[Western Karana]]. He wanders widely in the northeast quadrant of the zone. Tracking is highly recommended.

You say, 'Hail, Yiz Pon'

: Yiz Pon says, 'Argh... the [beasts] are on my tail.  They will find me soon... I gave them the [skull] and still they pursue me!'

You say, 'What skull?'

: Yiz Pon says, 'The skull of Wun Toque!  I have found it. And have learned the location of its eyes!  But now the [beasts] have it and I must flee...'

You say, 'What beasts?'

: Yiz Pon says, 'Here... No time left... Take this please... My brother [Hyrill] is staying in [Freeport].  Please... Ugh... Must keep moving...'

'''You receive [[Torn Parchment (Letter to Hyrill Pon)]] {{Item Lore|Letter to Hyrill Pon}}'''

[[A Splitpaw assassin]] spawns in the northeast zone corner and attacks Yiz Pon. 

:Yiz Pon says 'He has found me! Help meeeeeee!'

Kill [[a Splitpaw assassin]] and loot the [[Hollow Skull (Skull of Wun Toque)]]. Afterwards you can talk to Yiz more, though he doesn't have much else to say:

You say, 'Hail, Yiz Pon'

You say, 'Who is Hyrill?'

:Yiz Pon says, 'There is no time... must keep moving... ugh.'

You say, 'Where in Freeport?'

:Yiz Pon says, 'There is no time... must keep moving... ugh.'

Go to Yiz's brother [[Hyrill Pon]] in [[Freeport|West Freeport]], who can be found in the front bar of the Hogcaller's Inn. Give him the note:

: Hyrill Pon says, 'Peh!  He thinks this old skull he found is a legendary skull of Wun Toque.  It is said, a wizard who possesses one is granted power and intelligence far beyond those of his peers.  Yiz was searching for the skull's missing ruby eyes.  It seems he found the location of the first eye.  Hmm...  Lynuga...  Lynuga... I think I have heard that name before...  Yeah!  Now I remember.  I met her in the Foreign Quarter of Neria...  um...  Highpass Hold.  She was there trying to hawk some stolen gems!  I think she mumbled something about going home to Grobb.  I sure don't have time to track her down.'

<div class="facblock">
* Your faction with [[Commons Residents]] has been adjusted by 10.
* Your faction with [[The Freeport Militia]] has been adjusted by 5.
* Your faction with [[Knights of Truth]] has been adjusted by 5. (needs confirmation)
* Your faction with [[Priests of Marr]] has been adjusted by 5.
</div>
{{YouGainExperience}}

You now have to find two ruby eyes which need to be combined in the Hollow Skull container.

* The first eye is found on [[Lynuga]] in [[Innothule Swamp]], in the southeast corner. You may have to start a few new instances, as she is not always there. She is a level 32 [[Troll]] [[Shaman]] and doesn't present an easy fight. Loot a [[Large Ruby]] from her.

* The second eye is called a [[Ruby Pendant]] and can be found on a gnoll shaman named [[Kurrpok Splitpaw]] who spawns in [[Splitpaw Lair]] or [[Southern Karana]].

Put the two ruby eyes in the Hollow Skull and hit combine. This will turn into a [[Jeweled Skull]], which is a half decent held item.'''

